ut-gone drift explicitly rather than silently, extending the REG-GONE-001 flag to both directions with counts; (3) the 77/36 drift on this host is reconciled (rows added for real directories, dead rows removed) with before/after counts recorded. Related: REG-GONE-001 (inverse direction, complete), AUG-051 (auger-side workaround, auger board).", "acceptance_criteria": "a namespace created by POST /api/namespaces is listed by the immediately following GET /api/namespaces; the list flags drift in BOTH directions (on-disk-but-unlisted, listed-but-gone) with counts; the 77/36 drift measured on this host is reconciled with before/after counts recorded", "source": "auger foreman tick auger-2026-09-23-23-44-51 (AUG-051 root cause)", "files_changed": [], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "completed_at": null, "worker_status": null, "worker_summary": null, "dispatched_at": null, "foreman_note": "Filed cross-project from the auger tick that proved it. Reproduce: python3 /tmp/aug051_stale.py on /home/kara/auger (uses auger's transport for auth) - or POST then GET /api/namespaces with the DuckBrain key and look for the new name. Evidence: create=201, list present=False at t=0/5/10/.../55s; 133 listed vs 174 dirs on disk. Do NOT close this as a duplicate of REG-GONE-001 - that row is the opposite direction and is already complete.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "7c208e2dcb8077d8113b8fddb6e917e90a543bd5447f505f25f17f0d43a27d03"}}
