 {"id":"MUSTER-001","title":"Add Muster as an ADDITIONAL connection surface: point a muster server at DuckBrain's OpenAPI spec and get a generated CLI + MCP server + a unix-socket PROXY daemon, without changing or replacing the existing HTTP/MCP design (additive, owner directive)","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-24T09:22:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T09:22:06Z","source":"bane-directive 2026-09-24","reasoning":"OWNER DIRECTIVE (verbatim intent): \"add task for duckbrain to use a muster server so it has many connection options, this can be an additional server not killing the original design \u2014 so the proxy stuff.\" WHAT MUSTER IS (read from /home/kara/muster, README + AGENTS.md, 2026-09-24): muster turns any OpenAPI spec into multiple front-ends from one codebase \u2014 openapi-cli (humans), openapi-mcp (agents; the canonical and only MCP binary), openapi-daemon (multi-client, 'Unix socket proxy, shared state'), a Go library, Docker, WASM response plugins and a Starlark DSL. Repo is PRIVATE (github.com/wojons/muster, GOPRIVATE) so integration must not assume a public module fetch. WHY IT FITS: DuckBrain already PUBLISHES an OpenAPI spec \u2014 the daemon mounts '/api/ns/:ns/openapi.json' (src/cli/http.ts:491, createNamespaceOpenApiRoutes) and a hand-written spec exists at docs/../api/ns/hermes-memory/openapi.json. So muster can consume that spec AS-IS and synthesise a CLI, an MCP server and a proxy daemon over the same HTTP API \u2014 many connection options for one server, with zero new endpoints to hand-write. THE 'PROXY STUFF' IS THE DAEMON SURFACE: openapi-daemon is a Unix-socket proxy with shared state, i.e. a local connection point that multiplexes clients onto DuckBrain without each of them holding the API key and base URL \u2014 the same shape as the existing 'duckbrain ssh-connect' / unix-socket-served path (bin/duckbrain.js http --unix-socket=/tmp/duckbrain.sock), generalised and generated rather than hand-built. HARD CONSTRAINT \u2014 ADDITIVE ONLY: the current design stays the default and unchanged. HTTP :3000 with x-api-key auth, the stdio MCP server, and the namespace-scoped spec route must all keep working exactly as they do; muster is an OPTIONAL additional front-end, not a replacement, and must not become a required dependency of the daemon or the write path. Nothing in the serving path may import muster. WHY NOW: the release quorum round (2026-09-24) found the connection surface is narrow and unproven \u2014 the only live E2E we have drove DuckBrain through a hand-written crier bridge, and one of that round's findings (D5: GET /api/memories returns {items,total,...} while a client reading count/memories silently sees 0 rows) is exactly the class of spec/client drift a spec-driven generated surface would have caught for free. SCOPE GUARD: this row is the INTEGRATION ONLY. It does not cover fixing D5, D1 or the null-payload gate; those are separate rows and remain release blockers.","acceptance_criteria":["ADDITIVE PROOF: with muster absent or not installed, `node bin/duckbrain.js http --port 3000 --auth=apikey`, the stdio MCP server, and the full suite behave exactly as before \u2014 no new required dependency in package.json and no mustar/muster import anywhere under src/ (assert by grep).","`openapi-cli discover <duckbrain openapi spec>` parses DuckBrain's published spec with no error and `openapi-cli generate` produces typed commands covering the memory surface (POST /api/memories, GET /api/memories, GET /api/memories/key/*key).","The generated CLI performs a real remember -> recall round trip against a running daemon (x-api-key still the auth), and `--base-url` / MUSTER_BASE_URL can retarget it at another deployment without regenerating.","`openapi-mcp` fronting the same spec exposes the memory operations as MCP tools that an MCP client can list and call successfully; the tool list is asserted, not just the binary starting.","`openapi-daemon` (the unix-socket PROXY surface) accepts a client on its socket and proxies to DuckBrain, with no client needing the API key or the HTTP base URL directly; concurrent clients share it (the 'shared state' claim is exercised, not assumed).","A doc (docs/ or a section in docs/s3-native.md's neighbour) states the additional surfaces, the exact start commands, and the explicit statement that the existing HTTP/MCP paths are unchanged and remain the default.","Proven on the real bunker topology: agent + muster + DuckBrain on one box, driven over crier, with the 4-way reconciliation (crier / ledger / disk / S3) still clean \u2014 the generated surface must not change what lands in storage.","Negative: the daemon still refuses an unauthenticated write through the muster path (auth is not bypassed by adding a front-end) \u2014 assert 401, not just that the happy path works."],"notes":["Purely additive; if muster proves awkward, deleting it must leave DuckBrain byte-identical in behaviour.","Do not place a user-facing spec fetch on the write path; generation is a build/setup-time concern.","Related: the release test plan (duckbrain-release-testplan) L1 leg currently uses a hand-written crier bridge \u2014 a generated muster MCP surface is the natural replacement for that bridge in a later wave."],"attempts":0}
