 {"id": "DF-0925-04", "title": "P2 docs/api/mcp-tools.md does not document the recall asOf argument (DF-0924-03 open) and the HTTP API doc's as_of row gives no 410/400 error contract; usage skill has to carry the real wire semantics", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 1, "created_by": "dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "detail": "MCP recall accepts asOf (implemented + verified 09-24) yet mcp-tools.md recall schema omits it; http-api.md as_of row documents neither the 400 INVALID_CURSOR cursor forms nor 410 CHANGE_CURSOR_GONE resync behavior. Same-run evidence: 400 'cursor ordinal 99 does not name a committed change record', 410 'commit aaaa... no longer present' with guidance field. Fix direction: one doc pass over as_of/asOf + cursor errors in both API docs; keep skills/duckbrain-usage as the index."}
 {"id": "DF-0925-05", "title": "P2 Authorization change during an open SSE stream: auth store is hot-reloaded (auth/storeSchema.ts) but a revoked key's live subscription is only revoked lazily on the NEXT change event (hub.ts:651 re-check happens in deliver loop); a namespace with no writes keeps a revoked subscriber attached indefinitely", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "created_by": "dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "detail": "Live: swapped auth.json to {\"apiKeys\":[]} while an authorized subscriber was attached on an idle namespace — stream stayed open with heartbeats for the full 40s window (stream-rev.txt), no duckbrain.revoked.v1. Revocation DID apply before the next event (probe 401). Spec edge case says 'a revoked grant ends the stream' — with the current lazy re-check the end is event-driven, not revocation-driven. Fix direction: on auth-store reload, walk feeds and revoke subscribers whose principal no longer resolves."}
 {"id": "DF-0925-06", "title": "P3 duckbrain token --auth-file refuses to CREATE a store that does not exist ('must exist — refusing to fall back'), so a fresh agent following skills/duckbrain-usage 'Testing your changes safely' verbatim (mkdir + token mint) hits a hard error on first run", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 1, "created_by": "dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "detail": "node bin/duckbrain.js token --name=X --auth-file=<new path> errors '--auth-file not found ... refusing to fall back to the production ~/.duckbrain/auth.json' — the guard is correct for http but makes the documented scratch-bootstrap a two-step (create file with {\"apiKeys\":[]} then mint). Fix direction: allow token to create an empty store at an explicit path (keep the fatal guard for http), or fix the skill recipe to show the bootstrap step."}
